### A: single insteadOf, remote with pushurl
  fetch=http://127.0.0.1:7071/https/github.com/x/y  push=http://127.0.0.1:7071/https/github.com/x/y
fatal: repository 'http://127.0.0.1:7071/https/github.com/x/y/' not found
### A2: pushurl pointing at a different host
  fetch=http://127.0.0.1:7071/https/github.com/x/y  push=http://127.0.0.1:7071/https/evil.example.com/x/y
fatal: repository 'http://127.0.0.1:7071/https/evil.example.com/x/y/' not found
### B: insteadOf (fetch) + pushInsteadOf (push to a different endpoint), remote WITHOUT pushurl
  fetch=http://127.0.0.1:7071/F/github.com/x/y  push=http://127.0.0.1:7071/P/github.com/x/y
### B2: same config, remote WITH pushurl -> pushInsteadOf ignored, insteadOf applies
  fetch=http://127.0.0.1:7071/F/github.com/x/y  push=http://127.0.0.1:7071/F/github.com/x/y
fatal: repository 'http://127.0.0.1:7071/F/github.com/x/y/' not found
### C: explicit URL push and ls-remote (config A)
fatal: repository 'http://127.0.0.1:7071/https/github.com/x/explicit/' not found
fatal: repository 'http://127.0.0.1:7071/https/github.com/x/lsremote/' not found
### C2: explicit URL push with config B (pushInsteadOf applies to explicit URL?)
fatal: repository 'http://127.0.0.1:7071/P/github.com/x/explicitB/' not found
